.env
.session_cache/
data/
exports/
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch database/exports written by the CI-mode pipeline smoke test
# (tests/fixtures/ci_pipeline_config.yaml) and the reproducible-build
# script -- never the real project's data/ or exports/, but still not
# something to commit.
ci-build/
build/

# scripts/reproducible_build.py's scratch venv and build-manifest output.
.build-venv/
dist/

# Verified demo bundles from scripts/build_full_production_demo.py. Each run
# contains generated HTML/XLSX/JSON, a generated manifest and checksums, and
# a copy of the locked database -- all build output, none of it source.
demo-runs/

# Verified Coach Advantage bundles from scripts/build_coach_advantage_bundle.py.
# Same reasoning as demo-runs/ above -- all build output, none of it source.
coach-advantage-runs/

# Local scratch state from agent tooling; not part of the project.
.superpowers/

# Local GraphQL captures. The "full" file has real names; the "shapes" file
# has types only, but neither belongs in the repo.
apa-capture-full.json
apa-capture-shapes.json
apa-graphql-requests.json

# Output of scraper/full_apa_scrape.py -- sanitized (types only), but still
# generated output, not source.
scraper/sanitized_fixtures/

# The same directory name at the REPOSITORY ROOT, which is where the
# untracked apa_full_scrape.py draft (ignored below) writes. That draft calls
# its output "sanitized_fixtures" but keeps each GraphQL response's `data`
# verbatim -- real names and ids, not the type-only shapes
# scraper/full_apa_scrape.py produces. Only the path under scraper/ was
# ignored, so a root-level run would have left real identities
# untracked-but-committable. The directory already exists (created on import)
# and is currently empty; this closes the path rather than relying on it
# staying empty.
/sanitized_fixtures/

# Downloaded scoresheet PDFs from scraper/full_apa_scrape.py -- real league
# data (not sanitized like the fixtures above), never belongs in the repo.
scraper/scoresheets/

# Log file written by scraper/full_apa_scrape.py.
scraper/full_apa_scrape.log

# Local environments, test caches, and generated fixture archives.
venv*/
.pytest_cache/
scraper/sanitized_fixtures.zip

# Windows Explorer folder-customization metadata. Machine-local, never source.
desktop.ini

# Superseded local Playwright capture draft. Kept out of Git rather than
# moved under scraper/, because there is no approved implementation in it to
# move: scraper/full_apa_scrape.py already does this job properly, and this
# draft is strictly worse on the point that matters. Its
# sanitize_graphql_response() is a three-key whitelist that passes each
# response's entire `data` object through untouched, so every real player
# name and id survives into files it labels "sanitized"; the tracked module's
# summarize_shape() recursively replaces every value with its type name. The
# draft also hardcodes one real league/division id and drives the site
# automatically, which the tracked module deliberately does not do.
/apa_full_scrape.py

# Local Windows demo launchers. Not promoted to a tracked launcher because
# docs/demo_launcher.md specifies scripts/run_production_demo.py as a thin
# boundary around scripts/build_full_production_demo.py (neither implemented
# yet) and states that existing batch files "are not the unified launcher
# contract and must not be used as its source of truth". They are also
# non-portable (absolute path to one machine) and run_full_demo.bat's
# build_data_coverage.py step fails outright, since that script requires
# --opponent-team-id/--format/--session.
/run_demo.bat
/run_full_demo.bat
